WEBVTT

00:06.256 --> 00:07.424
<i>She's right there...</i>

00:08.550 --> 00:09.634
<i>Hina's in front of me.</i>

00:12.053 --> 00:13.972
What's going on, Mikey?

00:18.727 --> 00:19.853
<i>What'll I do?</i>

00:20.812 --> 00:21.730
Oh...

00:23.273 --> 00:24.107
Well...

00:27.986 --> 00:29.070
<i>This is so awkward.</i>

00:31.072 --> 00:33.491
Let's break up, Hina.

00:35.952 --> 00:37.704
<i>I dumped her without explanation.</i>

00:40.040 --> 00:41.332
I hate your guts!

00:42.292 --> 00:45.003
<i>What am I supposed to say to her now?</i>

00:49.716 --> 00:50.884
Got into another fight?

01:06.691 --> 01:09.152
TOKYO REVENGERS

02:33.695 --> 02:34.946
Dad!

02:39.200 --> 02:41.703
What did you say to Takemichi?

02:43.163 --> 02:44.289
Sorry, Hinata.

02:45.123 --> 02:47.709
But try to understand how I feel.

02:49.919 --> 02:52.755
I'd like you to fall for a guy
who's not a hoodlum.

02:53.923 --> 02:56.134
I want you to find happiness.

02:59.012 --> 03:02.223
Why did you fall in love with Mom?

03:03.474 --> 03:06.186
It wasn't for appearance's sake, right?

03:07.145 --> 03:09.355
I like Takemichi's character.

03:09.898 --> 03:13.151
He's a hoodlum
and doesn't look dependable,

03:13.234 --> 03:16.154
but he's actually very warm and kind.

03:16.237 --> 03:20.867
He's the kind of guy who'd help me
no matter what kind of pinch I'm in.

03:23.745 --> 03:27.040
You can't describe Takemichi
with just the word "hoodlum"!

03:27.916 --> 03:28.750
Hinata!

03:36.466 --> 03:39.260
<i>Dear God, hear my prayers.</i>

03:40.637 --> 03:43.473
Who prays at a shrine on Christmas?

03:43.556 --> 03:44.432
Huh?

03:45.266 --> 03:46.351
Emma?

03:46.434 --> 03:47.852
I thought it was you, Hina.

03:50.480 --> 03:52.941
You came to pray too, Emma?

03:53.024 --> 03:53.858
Yeah.

03:53.942 --> 03:58.238
My oldest brother used to
always come here to pray on Christmas.

03:58.321 --> 03:59.822
What a weirdo, huh?

04:00.406 --> 04:04.619
After I started going along with him,
it turned into an annual tradition.

04:04.702 --> 04:06.704
Wow, what a coincidence.

04:06.788 --> 04:09.666
I come to this shrine every Christmas too.

04:09.749 --> 04:11.417
Another weirdo.

04:12.335 --> 04:16.130
Then we may have met before.

04:17.632 --> 04:18.508
Maybe so.

04:19.801 --> 04:22.595
So, what did you pray for?

04:28.559 --> 04:32.146
I see. Your dad got involved, huh?

04:32.230 --> 04:35.316
That must have been brutal for Takemitchy.

04:35.400 --> 04:36.234
Yeah.

04:36.943 --> 04:39.529
But why'd he do it
just because your dad said to?

04:41.114 --> 04:41.990
I know!

04:43.241 --> 04:44.742
Leave this to me.

04:44.826 --> 04:45.660
Huh?

04:47.996 --> 04:50.123
Huh? Takemitchy?

04:50.957 --> 04:52.292
Mikey.

04:53.918 --> 04:57.088
Emma wants to know
if we know where Takemitchy is.

04:57.171 --> 04:58.172
No idea.

04:58.840 --> 05:00.216
We don't know.

05:01.926 --> 05:03.219
Huh? Look for him?

05:04.345 --> 05:05.596
What a pain.

05:05.680 --> 05:07.056
It's Christmas, you know?

05:07.682 --> 05:10.184
Well, you can get mad all you want.

05:10.768 --> 05:12.687
But I've got no idea where he might be.

05:12.770 --> 05:13.604
Draken.

05:15.064 --> 05:15.898
Let's go back.

05:17.108 --> 05:19.027
That Impulse I heard earlier...

05:19.110 --> 05:20.278
It was Mitsuya's.

05:21.529 --> 05:23.239
Takemitchy might be with him.

05:24.240 --> 05:26.993
Make sure you bring Takemitchy.

05:27.076 --> 05:28.828
Meet us at Hina's condo complex.

05:28.911 --> 05:29.912
What?

05:30.788 --> 05:32.790
Okay. Let's go, Hina.

05:32.874 --> 05:34.292
Huh? Wait!

05:35.084 --> 05:36.419
Takemichi's coming here?

05:36.502 --> 05:39.005
What? You love him, don't you?

05:39.088 --> 05:40.506
Tell him what you want to say.

05:40.590 --> 05:41.758
But...

05:43.760 --> 05:47.972
If I saw him now, I couldn't speak.
I might even cry.

05:48.056 --> 05:50.266
Hina!

05:50.892 --> 05:52.185
I'm sorry.

05:53.978 --> 05:59.192
I'm a hoodlum,
and I get what your dad means.

06:00.443 --> 06:02.862
And I've gotten you into danger.

06:06.866 --> 06:10.286
I couldn't stand it
if anything I did ever got you hurt.

06:10.870 --> 06:14.749
I promised that I'd rescue you.

06:16.250 --> 06:17.335
Rescue?

06:17.418 --> 06:18.711
Hina!

06:19.420 --> 06:24.175
I swear I'll protect you,
even if you were to die.

06:26.302 --> 06:29.722
What are you talking about, Takemichi?

06:31.766 --> 06:33.559
Even if you're hit by a truck...

06:34.811 --> 06:37.146
or you can't feel your legs anymore...

06:38.106 --> 06:40.566
I'll protect you every single time.

06:41.442 --> 06:42.276
Just please...

06:44.529 --> 06:45.571
Please...

06:46.697 --> 06:50.368
Forget that we ever broke up.

06:58.793 --> 06:59.752
Take me to the shrine...

07:02.046 --> 07:02.922
on New Year's.

07:03.798 --> 07:04.632
What?

07:06.134 --> 07:08.052
You mean...

07:09.929 --> 07:10.888
We've made up.

07:15.977 --> 07:16.978
Hina!

07:17.061 --> 07:19.355
Oh, please. Stop crying.

07:19.939 --> 07:20.773
I can't help it.

07:20.857 --> 07:22.817
I'm so happy for you, Hina.

07:22.900 --> 07:24.610
Why are you crying, Emma?

07:27.363 --> 07:30.032
He's weak with women and a weak fighter.

07:30.783 --> 07:33.119
But he's dependable
when the chips are down.

07:33.828 --> 07:38.082
Takemitchy really is like "him," isn't he?

07:39.834 --> 07:40.668
Yeah.

07:42.420 --> 07:43.337
Takemitchy.

07:45.256 --> 07:46.674
Let's take a ride together.

07:49.760 --> 07:51.554
Come on. Come on now.

07:51.637 --> 07:53.264
But Mikey.

07:53.347 --> 07:56.100
-I'm going to borrow Takemitchy for a bit.
-Looks like you lose.

07:56.184 --> 07:59.896
Oh, my. It sure is cold.
Let's go back inside.

08:01.314 --> 08:03.524
I'm so happy for you, Hina.

08:03.608 --> 08:06.986
Not so long ago, she was just
a little girl in elementary school.

08:08.237 --> 08:11.199
I guess this is how they grow up.

08:14.035 --> 08:17.288
If you interfere again,
Hinata will shut you out.

08:17.371 --> 08:19.248
I can't have that.

08:19.874 --> 08:22.585
But it's late, so I want her back in here.

08:30.468 --> 08:33.429
<i>When he's with the gang,
he's scary and hard to approach.</i>

08:34.180 --> 08:37.225
<i>But when it's just the two of us,</i>

08:37.808 --> 08:40.728
<i>he's so chill that I feel like
I could talk to him about anything.</i>

08:42.021 --> 08:43.648
Mikey, where are your parents?

08:43.731 --> 08:45.483
Huh? I don't have any.

08:45.566 --> 08:47.276
Me and Emma live with my grandpa.

08:47.360 --> 08:48.319
Really?

08:48.402 --> 08:50.780
Your grandpa raised you?
That's a surprise.

08:50.863 --> 08:52.615
Me and Emma have different moms.

08:53.241 --> 08:55.326
We used to live apart.

08:56.202 --> 09:00.498
About ten years ago, Emma's mom
left her with us and disappeared.

09:00.581 --> 09:02.917
Jeez, talk about brutal.

09:04.502 --> 09:07.129
My big brother was like our dad.

09:09.131 --> 09:12.760
<i>He was ten years older,
but we followed him everywhere.</i>

09:13.386 --> 09:14.887
<i>He taught us a lot.</i>

09:17.265 --> 09:18.683
Having him around was so natural...

09:19.892 --> 09:22.270
I sometimes feel lost without him.

09:25.982 --> 09:28.484
I can't understand what it means.

09:29.652 --> 09:33.197
At times like that, my mind goes blank.

09:34.198 --> 09:36.951
I completely lose my way in the world.

09:40.621 --> 09:44.125
I lose sight of the difference
between what's right and what's wrong.

09:45.585 --> 09:46.711
Mikey...

09:47.503 --> 09:53.384
<i>Mikey understands that he'll lose his mind
if he doesn't do something about it.</i>

09:54.135 --> 09:56.178
<i>He knows he bears a dark burden.</i>

10:03.019 --> 10:05.396
Even though my brother
was a biker gang leader,

10:05.479 --> 10:07.023
he was a poor fighter.

10:07.106 --> 10:09.900
What? No way! That's a huge surprise.

10:14.447 --> 10:17.533
<i>He inspired lots of guys.</i>

10:18.909 --> 10:20.328
<i>The hoodlums of Tokyo followed him</i>

10:21.037 --> 10:23.289
<i>even though they fought better than him.</i>

10:25.166 --> 10:26.167
Shinichiro.

10:27.084 --> 10:27.918
Yeah?

10:28.002 --> 10:30.171
You suck at fighting.

10:31.339 --> 10:33.174
You're always chasing women.

10:34.592 --> 10:35.926
Your farts reek.

10:38.429 --> 10:40.056
How come guys like you?

10:41.390 --> 10:43.559
You don't get it yet, Manjiro.

10:52.193 --> 10:54.862
<i>When he led the tough dudes of Tokyo,</i>

10:55.404 --> 10:57.406
<i>he was always a brilliant sight.</i>

10:58.949 --> 11:03.829
I bet they all thought they couldn't lose
as long as he had their backs.

11:03.913 --> 11:06.290
That's like you, Mikey.

11:09.543 --> 11:10.586
I'm weak.

11:11.087 --> 11:12.213
What?

11:15.341 --> 11:17.760
You're tough, Takemitchy.

11:20.930 --> 11:24.433
Winning fights isn't truly
what's most important.

11:25.685 --> 11:27.269
It's not losing to yourself.

11:29.647 --> 11:31.899
You're weak,
but you don't give in to anyone.

11:33.192 --> 11:35.736
You didn't even give in to BLACK DRAGON.

11:37.905 --> 11:42.118
When it looks like I'm about to lose heart
or when I'm about to lose my way,

11:42.702 --> 11:45.621
I want you to bawl me out, Takemitchy.

11:47.707 --> 11:48.833
Like my brother did.

11:57.758 --> 11:58.968
Of course, I will.

12:02.596 --> 12:07.268
We announcing that thing
at the first meeting of the new year?

12:07.351 --> 12:08.185
Yeah.

12:08.728 --> 12:10.730
Could start a lot of discontent.

12:11.397 --> 12:13.315
Then we'll just have to fight.

12:13.983 --> 12:16.235
As the twin dragons of Toman.

12:16.318 --> 12:17.945
Twin dragons?

12:18.529 --> 12:19.905
Brings back memories, huh?

12:25.786 --> 12:27.538
Want to go there now?

12:28.998 --> 12:31.083
It must've been cleaned off long ago.

12:32.960 --> 12:33.794
It's still here.

12:42.678 --> 12:45.097
<i>Luna. Mana.</i>

12:45.765 --> 12:48.392
<i>I left them alone,
but I hope they're okay.</i>

12:51.353 --> 12:52.730
That's pretty cool.

12:55.524 --> 12:57.276
What is that? A dragon?

12:57.359 --> 12:59.111
How long have you been there?

12:59.195 --> 13:00.988
I've been here the whole time.

13:01.655 --> 13:02.490
Uh...

13:05.034 --> 13:05.993
<i>He's a hoodlum.</i>

13:06.494 --> 13:08.370
<i>Just a kid, but he's wearing an earring.</i>

13:12.541 --> 13:13.918
Want some barbecue beef?

13:19.924 --> 13:20.925
Have a seat.

13:23.803 --> 13:26.597
My name's Ken Ryuguji. What's yours?

13:28.724 --> 13:30.059
Takashi Mitsuya.

13:30.392 --> 13:34.438
A kid like you on the streets this late,
your parents must be worried.

13:34.980 --> 13:36.398
You're a kid too.

13:37.107 --> 13:38.150
Who's he think he is?

13:38.818 --> 13:40.945
Hey, you ate all of it.

13:41.028 --> 13:44.114
Sorry. I haven't eaten all day.

13:45.825 --> 13:46.992
Okay.

13:47.076 --> 13:47.910
Huh?

13:49.870 --> 13:52.665
All right, this drawing is mine.

13:53.874 --> 13:55.376
Yours?

13:55.459 --> 13:57.586
In exchange for my barbecue beef.

13:58.879 --> 14:00.297
Come over to my place.

14:00.381 --> 14:01.340
Huh?

14:01.423 --> 14:02.675
You're not busy, right?

14:04.009 --> 14:07.179
What?

14:07.263 --> 14:08.681
This is your place?

14:08.764 --> 14:09.932
It's a whorehouse!

14:10.015 --> 14:11.851
Shut up, you brat!

14:11.934 --> 14:14.228
Ken, don't bring your friends here!

14:14.311 --> 14:15.229
Screw you.

14:18.107 --> 14:20.609
Ken, do some shopping for me.

14:20.693 --> 14:21.861
No, I'm busy.

14:21.944 --> 14:24.572
Ken, would you believe my last customer?

14:24.655 --> 14:25.948
Tell me later.

14:26.657 --> 14:28.868
Hey, Ken. Let's play poker.

14:28.951 --> 14:31.996
<i>What the heck is this place?
This is his home, right?</i>

14:32.830 --> 14:34.707
There. Full house.

14:34.790 --> 14:37.459
Amazing! This kid's a good player.

14:37.543 --> 14:40.379
No more wild jokers, okay?

14:40.462 --> 14:42.423
He keeps drawing them.

14:43.716 --> 14:46.218
From now on, your nickname is "Joker."

14:47.469 --> 14:49.972
Way to go, Mitsuya.
You're raking in the dough.

14:50.639 --> 14:53.058
You always earn spending money this way?

14:53.142 --> 14:56.353
Yeah. They pay me 1,000 yen
when they lose.

14:56.437 --> 14:58.606
I give them a free one-hour massage
when I lose.

14:58.689 --> 14:59.773
A massage?

14:59.857 --> 15:02.443
Ken's massages are top-notch.

15:02.526 --> 15:05.321
He soothes our tired bodies.

15:05.404 --> 15:07.990
This work is a lot tougher than it looks.

15:08.073 --> 15:10.492
It's hell when I keep losing.

15:10.576 --> 15:12.453
The next day, my hands are numb.

15:13.412 --> 15:14.288
Wow...

15:17.917 --> 15:19.710
What's wrong?

15:19.793 --> 15:24.131
I was just thinking how nice this is.

15:25.132 --> 15:28.594
My mom's never home.

15:29.178 --> 15:32.514
After school, all I ever do
is take care of my sisters.

15:32.598 --> 15:34.808
This guy's a runaway.

15:35.809 --> 15:36.644
Really?

15:37.144 --> 15:38.312
It'll be okay, Joker.

15:40.981 --> 15:42.733
I'd like to live here too.

15:45.486 --> 15:47.655
Ow! What was that for?

15:48.614 --> 15:49.782
Get out of here.

15:54.745 --> 15:57.247
You think this is fun, you dumb brat?

16:02.127 --> 16:04.296
Shit. What's her problem?

16:04.380 --> 16:06.298
Sorry, Mitsuya.

16:07.091 --> 16:11.470
But you see, they're not there
'cause they want to be.

16:14.515 --> 16:16.392
You like your mom's cooking?

16:16.475 --> 16:17.309
Huh?

16:18.727 --> 16:20.938
I think I'm a better cook.

16:21.438 --> 16:23.857
She hardly ever cooks, so it really sucks.

16:24.525 --> 16:25.442
I think I hate it.

16:25.526 --> 16:26.360
Really?

16:26.443 --> 16:27.820
Must be nice.

16:27.903 --> 16:28.737
Huh?

16:29.363 --> 16:31.615
Were you listening? It tastes awful.

16:33.075 --> 16:34.743
I don't have any parents.

16:35.953 --> 16:38.831
I wish I could say their cooking sucks.

16:40.791 --> 16:42.918
Go back home, Mitsuya.

16:43.752 --> 16:47.798
Truth is you're worried sick
about your sisters, aren't you?

16:49.216 --> 16:50.718
It's written all over your face.

16:53.012 --> 16:54.805
You're a good kid.

16:56.181 --> 16:57.766
You're not cut out to be a hoodlum.

16:57.850 --> 16:58.851
Later, man.

17:00.811 --> 17:03.772
<i>It's like he saw right through me.</i>

17:06.442 --> 17:07.651
I've found you.

17:07.735 --> 17:09.111
Ken Ryuguji.

17:09.194 --> 17:10.904
Huh? Mitsuya?

17:10.988 --> 17:12.406
Hey!

17:12.489 --> 17:15.117
One day, I will be your equal.

17:15.701 --> 17:17.161
I swear it.

17:18.037 --> 17:20.748
I will be a hoodlum
who cares for his family.

17:22.708 --> 17:23.751
What?

17:23.834 --> 17:25.419
-What?
-What?

17:27.588 --> 17:29.214
Why'd you get this tattoo?

17:29.298 --> 17:30.758
You grow your hair.

17:30.841 --> 17:31.675
Huh?

17:31.759 --> 17:34.178
I gave you
the barbecue beef for this, man.

17:34.261 --> 17:36.430
This dragon is mine.

17:45.064 --> 17:47.066
<i>Twin dragons, huh?</i>

17:47.775 --> 17:49.026
<i>Ever since then,</i>

17:49.109 --> 17:51.945
<i>I've been following him.</i>

17:52.654 --> 17:53.530
What's wrong?

17:53.614 --> 17:54.740
Nothing.

17:59.286 --> 18:00.579
Wow.

18:00.662 --> 18:02.039
It sure is crowded.

18:02.122 --> 18:03.457
It sure is.

18:03.540 --> 18:04.374
Takemitchy.

18:05.959 --> 18:08.837
Are you dressed for the children's fest?

18:08.921 --> 18:09.838
Yo.

18:09.922 --> 18:13.926
Wait, are you two Mitsuya's sisters?

18:14.009 --> 18:16.220
Yeah. This is Luna and Mana.

18:16.720 --> 18:19.640
How old are you? What little angels.

18:19.723 --> 18:22.059
Don't treat us like kids, dork face.

18:22.142 --> 18:23.018
Dork face.

18:23.102 --> 18:23.977
Huh?

18:24.478 --> 18:26.063
What a pretty lady.

18:26.146 --> 18:27.147
Pretty lady.

18:27.231 --> 18:29.233
Is that any way to raise children?

18:29.316 --> 18:30.859
Sorry, man.

18:31.443 --> 18:34.696
Yuzuha and Hakkai,
are your wounds better now?

18:34.780 --> 18:36.615
Yeah, all better.

18:36.698 --> 18:37.699
Right, Hakkai?

18:38.492 --> 18:39.368
Hey.

18:40.702 --> 18:41.537
Huh?

18:41.620 --> 18:43.789
Lady, can I hold your hand?

18:43.872 --> 18:45.124
Sure thing.

18:45.207 --> 18:46.708
Hold my hand too.

18:46.792 --> 18:48.127
Okay, we'll walk together.

18:48.210 --> 18:50.754
Hey, she's my Hina!

18:50.838 --> 18:54.633
How can you shout out loud
something so embarrassing?

18:54.716 --> 18:57.261
There goes my date.

18:57.344 --> 19:00.139
This was to make up for Christmas.

19:00.222 --> 19:01.765
Sorry, Takemitchy.

19:05.811 --> 19:08.188
You can go on a date anytime.

19:08.772 --> 19:10.190
Now I get it.

19:10.274 --> 19:12.109
No wonder you like him, Yuzuha.

19:13.110 --> 19:15.696
He was pretty badass that night.

19:19.199 --> 19:20.159
Taiju...

19:21.076 --> 19:23.287
<i>When he left a couple days ago, he said...</i>

19:23.787 --> 19:26.874
I wanted to raise Hakkai to be strong.

19:27.749 --> 19:29.751
It ticked me off when he was weak.

19:32.171 --> 19:34.089
Just who is Takemichi Hanagaki?

19:36.383 --> 19:39.595
Even though
I couldn't change Hakkai, he did.

19:40.596 --> 19:42.973
I'm not needed in this house anymore.

19:44.349 --> 19:45.976
I won't mend my ways.

19:46.768 --> 19:49.313
But I will admit
that violence isn't everything.

19:50.480 --> 19:52.191
This is goodbye, Yuzuha.

19:52.774 --> 19:54.276
You must be relieved.

20:00.574 --> 20:02.075
Taiju said that?

20:02.576 --> 20:03.410
Yeah.

20:04.286 --> 20:05.787
You know...

20:05.871 --> 20:08.832
He ended up changing both you and Taiju.

20:09.333 --> 20:13.212
To me, Takemichi Hanagaki is...

20:14.755 --> 20:15.797
What?

20:15.881 --> 20:20.260
Wait. Hold on here, Yuzuha.
Isn't it Taka you've got a crush on?

20:20.344 --> 20:21.929
Huh? Mitsuya?

20:22.012 --> 20:24.097
He's like a brother.
Besides, he's got short hair.

20:24.181 --> 20:26.725
What? You're in love with Takemitchy?

20:26.808 --> 20:29.311
Shut up, you moron!
Besides, he's got Hina.

20:31.271 --> 20:33.774
Nothing wrong
with a one-sided crush, right?

20:33.857 --> 20:35.234
Huh?

20:36.568 --> 20:37.653
What's wrong?

20:38.946 --> 20:40.447
-Nothing at all!
-Nothing at all!

20:40.530 --> 20:41.365
Huh?

20:41.990 --> 20:43.450
Oh, Takemichi.

20:43.533 --> 20:44.368
Yeah?

20:44.451 --> 20:45.786
They've got <i>ema.</i>

20:45.869 --> 20:47.329
Cool. Let's get one.

20:51.124 --> 20:51.959
Nice.

20:52.042 --> 20:53.460
What did you write?

20:54.920 --> 20:55.796
Hina.

20:55.879 --> 20:59.466
You know how they say
it won't come true if you show anyone.

20:59.549 --> 21:00.884
Hey, let us see.

21:00.968 --> 21:02.636
Show us, Takemitchy.

21:02.719 --> 21:03.804
No way!

21:03.887 --> 21:05.097
Why not?

21:05.180 --> 21:06.265
Show us, man.

21:06.974 --> 21:08.141
No way. Never!

21:08.225 --> 21:09.935
Hey, it's Takemitchy.

21:10.018 --> 21:11.603
What're you guys up to?

21:11.687 --> 21:15.315
Chifuyu, help me! You too, Peh-yan.

21:15.399 --> 21:17.442
What's the commotion?

21:17.526 --> 21:19.528
Sounds like fun.

21:20.445 --> 21:21.530
Cut that out, Hakkai!

21:21.613 --> 21:24.157
Give it back! That's my <i>ema.</i>

21:24.241 --> 21:26.368
Who's shouting "my Emma"?

21:26.451 --> 21:27.869
Oh, it's Takemitchy.

21:28.745 --> 21:29.579
Hakkai!

21:35.585 --> 21:37.254
Is this your <i>ema?</i>

21:42.050 --> 21:44.011
Please, give it back.

21:44.094 --> 21:46.596
Wow, you sure are desperate.

21:47.597 --> 21:48.640
What's going on?

21:48.724 --> 21:50.267
It's almost time.

21:50.350 --> 21:52.602
It's ten seconds until the new year.

21:53.228 --> 21:54.438
Let's jump together!

21:55.480 --> 21:57.149
Huh? What?

21:57.232 --> 21:58.358
-Three.
-Three.

21:58.442 --> 21:59.568
-Two.
-Two.

21:59.651 --> 22:01.236
-One.
-One.

22:02.279 --> 22:04.531
-Happy New Year!
-Happy New Year!

22:04.614 --> 22:07.367
I HOPE TO BECOME A HERO
WHO CAN SAVE EVERYONE.

23:30.575 --> 23:34.496
I never would have thought
Takemitchy could pull that off.

23:35.288 --> 23:36.248
Unexpected.

23:37.833 --> 23:39.876
But that won't be the end of this.

23:39.960 --> 23:41.002
Translation by Brian Athey
